  "decision_summary": "The query is palbociclib, a CDK4/6 inhibitor. The closest high-similarity evidence (ribociclib) shows moderate-to-high oral bioavailability in rats (37-55%) and dogs (64-87%) and is orally bioavailable in humans, supporting F >=20%. The low-F lead compound 1 (9.4% in rat) is structurally less optimized and lacks the acetyl/methyl/carbonyl substituents present in the query, so it is outweighed. Multiple less-similar human drugs with piperazine/heteroaromatic features also show high absolute F. Therefore predict high.",
